o v5.33.14</a>","+        <a href=\"security.html\" class=\"recommendation\">Security advisory:<br />Update to v5.33.16</a>","         <img class=\"logo\" src=\"assets/logo.png\" alt=\"logo\" />","         <div class=\"title\">systeminformation</div>","         <div class=\"subtitle\"><span id=\"typed\"></span>&nbsp;</div>","-        <div class=\"version\">New Version: <span id=\"version\">5.33.15</span></div>","+        <div class=\"version\">New Version: <span id=\"version\">5.33.16</span></div>","         <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light\" onclick=\"location.href = 'https://github.com/sebhildebrandt/systeminformation'\">View on Github <i class=\"fab fa-github\"></i></button>","       </div>","       <div class=\"down\">"],"additions":2,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/security.html","lines":["@@ -44,6 +44,20 @@","             <div class=\"col-12 sectionheader\">","               <div class=\"title\">Security Advisories</div>","               <div class=\"text\">","+                <h2>services() Command Injection Vulnerability</h2>","+                <p><span class=\"bold\">Affected versions:</span>","+                  &lt; 5.33.16<br>","+                  <span class=\"bold\">Date:</span> 2026-10-19","+                </p>","+","+                <h4>Impact</h4>","+                <p>We had an issue that on windows machines the service name passed to <span class=\"code\">services()</span> was inserted into a PowerShell command. The sanitizer removed ASCII quotes but kept unicode quotation marks like <span class=\"code\">“ ”</span>, which PowerShell also accepts as string delimiters. A crafted service name could break out of the filter string and execute PowerShell commands with the permissions of the node process.</p>","+","+                <h4>Patch</h4>","+                <p>Problem was fixed by removing unicode quotes and dashes in the sanitizer and by allowing only a whitelist of characters for windows service names. If you are using version 5, please upgrade to version >= 5.33.16.</p>","+                <hr>","+                <br>","+","                 <h2>networkStats() Path Traversal Vulnerability</h2>","                 <p><span class=\"bold\">Affected versions:</span>","                   &lt; 5.33.14<br>"],"additions":14,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/v6/audio.html","lines":["@@ -2,26 +2,26 @@"," <html lang=\"en\">","   <head>","     <!-- Required meta tags -->","-    <meta charset=\"utf-8\">","-    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, shrink-to-fit=no\">","+    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />","+    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, shrink-to-fit=no\" />"," ","     <!-- CSS -->","-    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://stackpath.bootstrapcdn.com/bootstrap/4.1.3/css/bootstrap.min.css\" integrity=\"sha384-MCw98/SFnGE8fJT3GXwEOngsV7Zt27NXFoaoApmYm81iuXoPkFOJwJ8ERdknLPMO\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\">","-    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://pro.fontawesome.com/releases/v5.15.1/css/all.css\" integrity=\"sha384-9ZfPnbegQSumzaE7mks2IYgHoayLtuto3AS6ieArECeaR8nCfliJVuLh/GaQ1gyM\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\">","-    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../roboto/css/roboto.css\">","-    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\">","+    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://stackpath.bootstrapcdn.com/bootstrap/4.1.3/css/bootstrap.min.css\" integrity=\"sha384-MCw98/SFnGE8fJT3GXwEOngsV7Zt27NXFoaoApmYm81iuXoPkFOJwJ8ERdknLPMO\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\" />","+    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://pro.fontawesome.com/releases/v5.15.1/css/all.css\" integrity=\"sha384-9ZfPnbegQSumzaE7mks2IYgHoayLtuto3AS6ieArECeaR8nCfliJVuLh/GaQ1gyM\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\" />","+    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../roboto/css/roboto.css\" />","+    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\" />","     <script src=\"main.js\"></script>"," ","     <!-- Favicon -->","-    <link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/png\" sizes=\"192